---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Same law. Less work."
  description="A simple proposal: stop using solid black boxes when the law doesn’t require it. Improve readability, reduce labor, and preserve public trust."
>
  <section class="section">
    <p class="kicker">Phase 0 launch</p>
    <h1 class="h1">Same law. Less work.</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      Rethink Redaction promotes clear, lawful, and accessible redaction practices — so public records remain readable
      while protected information stays protected.
    </p>

    <div style="display:flex; gap:.75rem; flex-wrap:wrap; margin-top: 1.25rem;">
      <a class="btn" href="/about">What this is</a>
      <a class="btn" href="/faq">Read the FAQ</a>
      <a class="btn" href="/contact">Contact</a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="grid grid-3">
      <div class="card" style="padding:1.25rem;">
        <h2 class="h2">Clarity</h2>
        <p class="small">
          Redaction should protect sensitive data without destroying comprehension. Layout matters.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="card" style="padding:1.25rem;">
        <h2 class="h2">Compliance</h2>
        <p class="small">
          We focus on what laws typically require: protect the right fields, not the entire page.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="card" style="padding:1.25rem;">
        <h2 class="h2">Efficiency</h2>
        <p class="small">
          Better redaction workflows can reduce staff time, printing waste, and needless friction.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="card" style="padding: 1.5rem;">
      <h2 class="h2">What you’ll find here</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>We Are At Phase 0 as of 3/3 3:33am PST </li>
        <li>Plain-language guidance and examples (Phase 1)</li>
        <li>Downloadable templates and checklists (Phase 1)</li>
        <li>A public “design-first” framing of readability and trust</li>
        <li> Updates Are Coming </li>
      </ul>
      <p class="small">
        This Phase 0 site is intentionally minimal. It exists to be linkable, legible, and launch-ready.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>